  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the digits are not allowed to repeat in any number formed by using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the number of all numbers greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to __________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "96",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have to form a number greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn></math>&nbsp;by using the digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence, the first place of the number can&#39;t be zero.</p><p>Thus, for the first place we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;choices i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and the remaining places can be filled with any of the digits, thus&nbsp;we have respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;choices.</p><p>Hence, using the fundamental principle of multiplication, the total numbers which are greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn></math>&nbsp;are</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d71239ae-9ae1-4f58-9f50-1318ef46fcaf-image.png\" style=\"width: 222px; height: 73px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
